    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 **66 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag as a creation-fixed boolean, mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern in this OfficeFloor pipeline codebase. The flag is `true` when the owner's city already held **40\u201349** owners at creation time (approaching the limit of 50); the hard 409 rejection at 50 is untouched.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n2. **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `capacity_warning` column so the entity persists.\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `capacityWarning` (boolean, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` response schema; the generated `OwnerDto` and MapStruct pick it up by name, so it surfaces on GET.\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"capacityWarning\", ignore = true)` on the write mapping (it's a derived/read-only field, never bound from the request).\n5. **`AssignCapacityWarning.java`** (new function) \u2014 runs on the built `@Val Owner`, counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive) via `OwnerRepository`, and sets the flag when `count >= 40 && count < 50`. Since it runs before `SaveOwner`, the count excludes the owner being created, and the hard rejection has already fired for full cities.\n6. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `capacityWarning` step into the create pipeline (after `bulkSignupWarning`, before `customerCode`), under the same `transaction` governance as its neighbors.\n\nThe new `Cp54Tests` (warning), `Cp18Tests` (hard-limit unchanged), and `Cp22Tests` (bulk-warning) all pass, along with the entire suite.",
